# Normalise line endings in the repository by default.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not execute on POSIX systems.
*.sh text eol=lf

# ── DO NOT TOUCH THESE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The vendored original test suite is hashed at import and must be byte-identical
# on every platform. If git converts its line endings on checkout, the SHA-256
# values change and the tamper check fails — which looks exactly like we edited
# the tests. Marking them binary (-text) disables all conversion.
#
# The manifest itself must also stay LF: `sha256sum -c` parses filenames to the
# end of line, so a trailing CR makes every path unreadable.
tests/original/**    -text
tests/original.sha256 -text

# The parity digests are compared byte-for-byte against C program output.
tests/parity/expected_digests.txt -text
